Narcis is a port of Jonquil (https://github.com/b12n-oss/jonquil), pinned
at commit 0ac90991 (v0.4.4). Copyright 2026 the Jonquil authors. Jonquil is
distributed under the Eclipse Public License 2.0 (see LICENSE). UPSTREAM.md
lists, file by file, what Narcis lifted from Jonquil and what changed.

Jonquil ports and adapts DrClojure by Kim Taegyoon
(https://github.com/kimtg/DrClojure-Neo), distributed under the Eclipse
Public License 1.0. Code in Narcis that descends from DrClojure through
Jonquil keeps that lineage, and UPSTREAM.md records which files it is in.
Both were received under the Eclipse Public License 1.0 and are
distributed here, with Narcis's own code, under the Eclipse Public
License 2.0, as section 7 of EPL-1.0 allows once a new version of the
licence is published.

The buffer's text structure is eve.text, part of Eve
(https://github.com/SeniorCareMarket/eve, libs/eve-text), whose two
source files are carried in this repo under src/eve/
unchanged (UPSTREAM.md gives their hashes). eve.text is a port of
CodeMirror 6's Text data structure (@codemirror/state, Marijn Haverbeke
and contributors, MIT License).

Narcis runs on Eve and on the Jolt runtime
(https://github.com/jolt-lang/jolt), both distributed under the Eclipse
Public License 2.0. Neither is included in this repo; deps.edn names the
Eve pin, and UPSTREAM.md names the rest.

Six of the colour themes in src/narcis/theme.clj (lifted from Jonquil)
take their colours from popular editor themes. The themes use their
published colour values, mapped to Narcis's token kinds, and include none
of their source. Each theme's find-highlight tint is Jonquil's own, and
any other colour that differs from the original is noted beside its
theme:

- Gruvbox Dark and Light: Gruvbox by morhetz, MIT/X11
  (https://github.com/morhetz/gruvbox, colors/gruvbox.vim).
- Dracula: Dracula Theme, MIT
  (https://github.com/dracula/emacs, dracula-theme.el).
- Nord: Nord by Sven Greb, MIT (https://github.com/nordtheme/nord,
  src/nord.css, and the comment colour from https://github.com/nordtheme/vim).
- Zenburn: the original Zenburn by Jani Nurminen (GNU GPL), with the palette
  as https://github.com/bbatsov/zenburn-emacs publishes it.
- Monokai: the original Monokai by Wimer Hazenberg, with the palette as
  https://github.com/oneKelvinSmith/monokai-emacs publishes it.

Six more themes take their colours the same way:

- Tokyo Night: tokyonight.nvim by folke, Apache-2.0
  (https://github.com/folke/tokyonight.nvim, lua/tokyonight/colors/night.lua
  and storm.lua).
- Catppuccin Mocha and Latte: Catppuccin, MIT, copyright 2021 Catppuccin
  (https://github.com/catppuccin/palette, palette.json).
- One Dark: onedark.vim by Joshua Dick, MIT
  (https://github.com/joshdick/onedark.vim, autoload/onedark.vim). Its
  comment grey is Jonquil's #666f7e, a little lighter than the original
  #5c6370, so that it meets the contrast floor.
- Kanagawa: kanagawa.nvim by Tommaso Laurenzi, MIT
  (https://github.com/rebelot/kanagawa.nvim, lua/kanagawa/colors.lua).
- Rosé Pine: Rosé Pine, MIT
  (https://github.com/rose-pine/neovim, lua/rose-pine/palette.lua).
